oo tiles first.\n\nReason: Discarding W7 is safe because it's a singleton and not contributing to any potential sequence in my hand. It also starts the process of reducing suits to achieve a Half Flush (Bamboo + honors). F3 could be kept temporarily as it might form a pung if I draw more (3 F3 left in wall per unshown tiles), but it's less likely and not a high-value wind for me. T1, T2, T3 are a valuable Chow that gives me one meld already, so I should keep them. T8 and T9 pairs are good for potential pungs or chows (T7-T8-T9 or T8-T9 with T7). So W7 is the least useful tile now.\n\nAnswer: Play W7"}
